WEBVTT

00:16.750 --> 00:20.370
I hate the Magia Vander.

00:20.740 --> 00:23.630
Because of the spell Albis Vina cast,

00:23.630 --> 00:25.880
Will is always chasing after her.

00:25.880 --> 00:30.800
Yet she doesn't do a thing. She's merely 
waiting in the tower, and that's just...

00:31.700 --> 00:33.440
I feel so sorry for Will.

00:34.600 --> 00:36.450
<i>I know.</i>

00:36.450 --> 00:39.140
<i>I know I put a spell on him.</i>

00:40.130 --> 00:42.150
<i>And because of that magic...</i>

00:42.150 --> 00:47.400
<i>Because of the curse I cast, 
Will's been wounded and suffered so much.</i>

00:48.570 --> 00:50.650
<i>Ever since those tears that started it all...</i>

00:54.910 --> 00:58.660
<i>Just how much have I made you cry?</i>

00:59.910 --> 01:02.160
<i>Should I have gone on a rampage instead?</i>

01:02.920 --> 01:04.920
<i>Should I have run away?</i>

01:05.730 --> 01:08.070
<i>Should I have pretended 
not to know anything</i>

01:08.070 --> 01:10.930
<i>and gone to hold you in my arms?</i>

01:20.830 --> 01:22.350
You've got it all wrong.

01:25.590 --> 01:28.250
I don't hate you, Elfie.

01:29.870 --> 01:33.700
In fact, it's my fault you're all alone.

01:34.730 --> 01:36.760
If I were to hate anyone...

01:37.330 --> 01:41.470
it would be me, 
the no-talent Will Serfort.

01:44.350 --> 01:46.180
Which is why I must be quick

01:46.630 --> 01:48.200
and hurry to where you are, Elfie.

01:49.460 --> 01:54.760
I want to stand beside you, Elfie... 
and fulfill our precious promise.

01:56.210 --> 01:58.400
<i>It's because you say things like that,</i>

01:58.940 --> 02:02.390
<i>because you smile at me 
even when we're apart,</i>

02:03.520 --> 02:05.730
<i>that I decided to hold 
myself back and endure this.</i>

02:06.680 --> 02:10.630
<i>So that I wouldn't break our promise
and I could say I've waited for you.</i>

02:10.990 --> 02:14.820
Please, Cerri! No, magnificent 
Professor Cerridwen!

02:14.820 --> 02:16.990
Please guide Will!

02:16.990 --> 02:18.200
My, my!

02:18.200 --> 02:21.370
<i>Although there have been times
 I secretly pulled some strings.</i>

02:22.310 --> 02:24.370
<i>You've been faithfully chasing after me.</i>

02:25.110 --> 02:27.380
<i>What is there that I can do for you?</i>

02:28.040 --> 02:31.630
<i>I want to be of help to you.</i>

02:32.340 --> 02:37.390
I'm sure <i>that's</i> what that Magia Vander
 with a head full of flowers is thinking!

02:37.390 --> 02:43.680
I want to help Will too,
 Professor Workner!

02:42.110 --> 02:46.010
In this state, I'm impressed you'd say
 someone <i>else</i> has a head full of flowers.

02:46.780 --> 02:47.740
As for the rest of you,

02:47.740 --> 02:51.530
you were accepted by factions, but now 
you've gone and snuck out of the tower.

02:51.530 --> 02:54.300
I don't want to leave Will yet.

02:54.300 --> 02:56.920
My own position is 
of secondary importance.

02:59.690 --> 03:02.990
Hey, what's going on with you? 
You're acting strangely.

03:02.990 --> 03:04.840
W-Worry not.

03:04.840 --> 03:07.590
I merely fled the faction 
as though my life depended on it.

03:08.630 --> 03:11.050
Hold on! What's wrong, Lihanna?

03:12.740 --> 03:16.730
The cook-pot... I mean, 
the Witch of the Hammer is on the move.

03:16.730 --> 03:19.550
If we leave things to her, 
Will and Julius will be just fine.

03:19.550 --> 03:21.210
The Witch of the Hammer?

03:21.210 --> 03:24.390
You can't mean the one from 
the seven legends of the academy.

03:24.390 --> 03:26.450
We can't just leave this to someone else!

03:26.450 --> 03:28.160
You know I'm onto you, don't you?

03:28.160 --> 03:30.560
Professor Workner, 
you're worried about Will.

03:30.910 --> 03:33.230
You keep visiting the tower
like a long-distance wife!

03:33.230 --> 03:34.970
Even if you get turned away at the gate.

03:34.970 --> 03:37.090
Don't say it in a way
that invites misunderstanding!

03:37.090 --> 03:38.820
How do you even know about that?

03:38.820 --> 03:40.480
Miss Clairie told me!

03:41.340 --> 03:43.330
That blabbermouth classmate of mine!

03:43.330 --> 03:45.740
We want to help Will as well.

03:45.740 --> 03:47.800
There's no need to take action.

03:47.800 --> 03:48.710
Sion?

03:48.710 --> 03:50.390
What are you saying?

03:50.390 --> 03:54.340
Didn't you come here so that 
you could help rescue Will, too?

03:54.340 --> 03:57.340
I came to ensure that you lot
didn't do anything unnecessary.

03:57.340 --> 03:58.840
To keep an eye on you.

03:59.760 --> 04:03.600
He was told over and over it couldn't 
be done, but look how far he's come.

04:03.990 --> 04:06.980
Even when I wasn't watching, 
he clumsily clawed his way through

04:06.980 --> 04:08.730
and overcame every hurdle.

04:09.410 --> 04:11.140
All we need to do is wait.

04:11.140 --> 04:13.800
He will overcome this, too. Besides...

04:14.510 --> 04:17.990
if someone swoops in now, he won't be
 able to show off what he can do, right?

04:18.880 --> 04:20.850
Do you mean as a mage?

04:23.980 --> 04:25.920
As a man.

04:42.010 --> 04:46.720
Episode 22
Hoping, Blooming, Thundering

06:17.770 --> 06:19.230
Emma Klever,

06:19.230 --> 06:21.490
I grant you the blessing of wind.

06:26.990 --> 06:30.490
<b>Emma Klever
Accepted into the Wind Faction</b>

06:29.330 --> 06:30.490
I did it!

06:32.750 --> 06:34.250
Mike Maius,

06:34.250 --> 06:35.990
come join the Dark Faction.

06:36.580 --> 06:40.710
<b>Mike Maius
Accepted into the Dark Faction</b>

06:39.650 --> 06:43.010
All right! Here we go!

06:47.270 --> 06:49.850
Lyril Mars! Gordon Vally!

06:49.850 --> 06:52.600
Both of you, proceed to the fire faction!

06:52.600 --> 06:55.600
Yeah! We did it!

06:52.680 --> 06:55.600
<b>Lyril Mars & Gordon Vally
Accepted in the Fire Faction</b>

06:56.020 --> 06:57.600
So you finally made it, huh?

06:59.350 --> 07:01.040
Okay, congratulations!

07:00.470 --> 07:05.360
We did it! Finally!

07:01.040 --> 07:04.930
Everyone who has received a blessing, 
please report to your respective factions.

07:05.970 --> 07:08.060
While increasing our numbers is necessary,

07:08.060 --> 07:11.110
each faction's standards 
for acceptance are far too lax.

07:11.110 --> 07:13.370
These so-called mages 
are fresh out of the academy.

07:13.690 --> 07:16.500
Dullard. You know that's not 
the name of the game here.

07:16.500 --> 07:19.010
After the Terminalia incident,

07:19.010 --> 07:22.760
those overlooked by our scouts 
have become more adaptable.

07:23.400 --> 07:24.910
Though from my perspective,

07:24.910 --> 07:26.800
they are still of an inferior race.

07:27.510 --> 07:30.550
Each of them has transformed 
the unknown into the known.

07:31.380 --> 07:33.290
I knew pushing them to the brink was good.

07:33.290 --> 07:37.060
Even immature fledglings can become 
migratory birds, soaring through the sky.

07:37.500 --> 07:41.320
And so the Second Bloom is about 
to come to an end too, but...

07:41.600 --> 07:43.570
Will and Julius haven't arrived yet!

07:43.880 --> 07:46.320
At this rate, they'll end up disqualified!

07:46.880 --> 07:49.830
Any more of this would be 
a simple waste of time.

07:49.830 --> 07:54.580
It's likely they failed to form a plan,
fell into despair, and ran away.

07:54.580 --> 07:57.330
How can you say that when you're 
the one standing in their way?

07:57.870 --> 08:02.680
Those who'd flee this hell of diligence
have no right to ascend the tower.

08:02.680 --> 08:06.360
We of the Upper Institute 
will take guardianship of them.

08:07.070 --> 08:09.840
I trust you have no objections, 
Lady Elfaria?

08:16.130 --> 08:18.600
We're sorry we're late!

08:20.720 --> 08:22.340
Julius Reinberg!

08:22.340 --> 08:23.730
Will Serfort!

08:23.730 --> 08:25.150
Present!

08:26.990 --> 08:28.000
Will!

08:28.000 --> 08:28.990
And Julius!

08:31.720 --> 08:34.240
How dare a mere lab rat cause 
such unnecessary trouble.

08:35.740 --> 08:38.500
The selection requirements 
are the same as last time!

08:38.880 --> 08:40.750
Your qualification
as a wand is in question!

08:43.020 --> 08:47.510
Will Serfort, honored Magia Vander...
 I trust this is acceptable.

08:51.740 --> 08:52.920
Fine by me.

08:55.710 --> 08:56.600
Yes, sir!

08:57.800 --> 09:00.010
<i>Will he really be all right?</i>

09:00.010 --> 09:05.020
<i>After all of that, I still haven't 
the faintest idea if he can control Wis.</i>

09:05.400 --> 09:08.530
<i>Would it be better if I lent him 
my magic without getting caught?</i>

09:13.290 --> 09:16.260
Julius, I grant you a blessing.

09:16.260 --> 09:18.290
Don't try anything. Just come here.

09:18.580 --> 09:20.790
Lady Elfaria! But that's...

09:21.070 --> 09:23.950
Thank you for lending Will your power.

09:23.950 --> 09:26.550
You should believe in him, too. Trust Will.

09:36.740 --> 09:40.310
If you waste all the hard work I put in, 
I'll never forgive you. Understand?

09:40.730 --> 09:42.710
Thank you, Julius!

09:43.630 --> 09:45.560
<i>Wait for me, Elfie!</i>

09:48.160 --> 09:49.160
Begin.

09:49.860 --> 09:55.130
Through my magic, the path 
to Wis should already be open.

09:56.380 --> 09:59.570
You should understand the process now.

10:02.150 --> 10:04.220
So show me, won't you?

10:04.220 --> 10:06.230
Show me a brand new world for a sword.

10:07.430 --> 10:08.670
<i>Picture it.</i>

10:09.610 --> 10:11.030
<i>A single book.</i>

10:15.920 --> 10:17.320
<i>Remember.</i>

10:19.370 --> 10:20.670
<i>Find it.</i>

10:20.980 --> 10:22.230
<i>Carve it deep!</i>

10:22.970 --> 10:25.230
<i>Retracing the path you've traveled 
to reach today...</i>

10:27.730 --> 10:30.110
<i>recall the fragments you need now!</i>

10:30.790 --> 10:32.620
Memory charge complete!

10:33.110 --> 10:36.330
Tearis Wis: Reload!

10:39.490 --> 10:40.400
What?

10:41.170 --> 10:42.500
A blade of light?

10:42.500 --> 10:45.490
No, a sword of ice magic?

10:45.490 --> 10:46.500
Impossible.

10:46.790 --> 10:49.250
He was able to produce Wis on his own?

10:56.300 --> 10:57.640
<b>Glauss Wis</b>

10:57.720 --> 11:01.010
<b><u>Mageblade</u>

 You want to know about mageblades? They're just as you see them. 
They lap up magic and make its power their own. 
A skill meant to slaughter mages? Ha ha! You have it all wrong! 
They're a last resort for doing something about this lost cause of a world. 

-With a smile from a certain member of the little people</b>

11:01.260 --> 11:02.520
<b>Tearis Wis</b>

11:02.680 --> 11:06.020
<b><u>Memory Charge </u>

The power of emotion is a wonderful thing, isn't it? It can transform the magic you were struck by
 on some long ago day into power that is your own, even if it the event was sad or painful. 
Or something like that! I don't really understand it well myself! 
The one thing that's for certain is that every memory, even your story about to be written...
 If you don't make full use of all of it, there will be no way to protect this world. 
-A certain giddy Witch of the Hammer</b>

11:06.980 --> 11:09.680
<i>You cast a spell on me.</i>

11:10.840 --> 11:13.670
<i>But it wasn't a curse.</i>

11:14.600 --> 11:16.110
<i>We initiated it together...</i>

11:16.670 --> 11:18.640
<i>The spell known as a promise.</i>

11:19.580 --> 11:22.240
<i>Right now, you feel like you haven't
been able to do anything,</i>

11:22.240 --> 11:25.120
<i>so you might have come to hate yourself.</i>

11:25.810 --> 11:27.340
<i>But that's not right.</i>

11:27.340 --> 11:29.130
<i>It's not right at all, Elfie!</i>

11:29.770 --> 11:32.130
<i>You've given me so much.</i>

11:32.690 --> 11:35.630
<i>You've given me infinite courage.</i>

11:36.310 --> 11:38.460
<i>So, here at the end, 
I want you to hold out.</i>

11:39.460 --> 11:42.120
<i>Here at the end, 
I want to try to look good.</i>

11:43.340 --> 11:46.050
<i>Up to today, you've given me so much...</i>

11:48.830 --> 11:50.270
<i>And now I want to come to you.</i>

12:02.470 --> 12:03.540
He's strong!

12:03.620 --> 12:07.710
<b>Lightning Faction Aide-de-Camp
Guilford Zurgas</b>

12:03.940 --> 12:07.790
It seems weaker than when he charges it
 from an external source, but...

12:08.190 --> 12:11.360
Even so, its destructive power exceeds 
that of intermediate-level magic.

12:11.870 --> 12:13.550
This is a surprise.

12:20.530 --> 12:22.350
<i>Put your feelings into it!</i>

12:23.950 --> 12:25.810
<i>Pour them into your sword!</i>

12:28.700 --> 12:29.600
Will!

12:30.190 --> 12:32.110
I like it!

12:32.410 --> 12:35.610
Full marks. You've earned 
a smiley face, Will.

12:37.030 --> 12:39.120
Since it was you who sent him
 up to the tower,

12:39.120 --> 12:41.520
I've respected your wishes 
and merely observed.

12:41.890 --> 12:44.700
But you've done very well, Cerridwen.

12:45.830 --> 12:49.540
Or should I say... Magical Academy 
Headmistress Caldron?

12:50.280 --> 12:54.010
When I'm in this form, 
could you please call me Cerridwen?

12:54.010 --> 12:56.900
Casting aging magic on myself 
is exhausting, you know?

12:56.900 --> 12:59.070
The truth is I'm still young 
and perky, after all.

13:00.300 --> 13:04.570
Also, this place is forbidden to anyone 
other than mages, you realize?

13:06.120 --> 13:08.520
A little late to point that out,
 no, Ageless Witch?

13:08.520 --> 13:12.770
Besides, you've been working
 behind the scenes, too.

13:13.410 --> 13:18.280
It was you who gave the dwarves
that rare Wist gem, wasn't it?

13:18.580 --> 13:21.050
He's a new user of the fifth element.

13:21.470 --> 13:25.280
You could look the other way
over such a small present, couldn't you?

13:25.280 --> 13:28.540
His capacity is still developing.

13:28.540 --> 13:30.160
As reloading with his own power goes,

13:30.160 --> 13:31.970
his energy amplification is still sloppy.

13:32.870 --> 13:36.960
But with Wist-set silver reinforcement,
it works more than well enough.

13:38.010 --> 13:40.900
His hair turning white and 
his loss of memory...

13:40.900 --> 13:44.210
When it comes to using a mageblade,
Will's been too green thus far.

13:44.210 --> 13:46.180
He paid a heavy price.

13:46.450 --> 13:49.770
But now, after six years 
of growing at the academy,

13:50.180 --> 13:53.070
I can finally teach him 
all sorts of things.

13:58.540 --> 14:03.610
<i>Will you be the one to show us the 
unknown that Cerridwen seeks?</i>

14:09.580 --> 14:11.120
<i>I can't wait to see.</i>

14:12.790 --> 14:13.910
...can't be.

14:14.510 --> 14:15.130
What?

14:15.550 --> 14:16.380
This can't be.

14:16.850 --> 14:23.380
This can't be, this can't be, this can't be,
 this can't be, this can't be...

14:23.380 --> 14:25.640
This can't be!

14:28.280 --> 14:29.640
Lord Kreutz?

14:30.510 --> 14:32.140
He defeated the creatures.

14:32.870 --> 14:34.500
That output...

14:34.500 --> 14:37.900
isn't something
 the dwarves could produce.

14:38.490 --> 14:42.150
So you get it at last, do you? 
His absolute foolishness.

14:53.930 --> 14:56.070
<i>It reverted to its original form.</i>

14:56.850 --> 15:01.600
<i>When I fuel it myself, the energy 
depletes far faster than a regular charge.</i>

15:02.090 --> 15:03.730
<i>I need to use it carefully.</i>

15:04.170 --> 15:05.870
Not yet...

15:05.870 --> 15:08.300
We mustn't acknowledge him yet!

15:08.300 --> 15:10.180
We cannot call something like that magic!

15:10.480 --> 15:13.680
Kreutz, you're just 
nit-picking now, aren't you?

15:13.680 --> 15:16.940
In what way? If this unknown 
cannot be explained,

15:16.940 --> 15:18.810
should he be allowed
to call himself a mage?!

15:19.280 --> 15:23.150
And what of the possibility 
that the sword is a magic item?

15:23.150 --> 15:27.070
During a Bloom, equipment
other than wands is strictly forbidden!

15:27.070 --> 15:30.480
Even if we establish that 
he hasn't violated the rules,

15:30.480 --> 15:33.830
there is still a need
 to carefully examine Will Serfort!

15:34.320 --> 15:36.580
That's true enough.

15:37.050 --> 15:39.830
But if one thinks of his sword
 as his wand...

15:40.110 --> 15:43.130
Either way, it's true that 
there is no precedent for this.

15:43.130 --> 15:45.590
We must be cautious 
as we get to the bottom of it.

15:46.110 --> 15:48.220
He's come this far, 
and they're still arguing?

15:48.500 --> 15:52.560
It shows just how much of an 
outlier they find Will Serfort to be.

15:52.860 --> 15:57.040
Even the high mages of each faction 
cannot decide how to handle him.

15:58.540 --> 16:00.840
<i>The only ones who can bring 
this place under control</i>

16:00.840 --> 16:04.050
<i>are those who stand at the pinnacle 
of the tower, the Magia Vander.</i>

16:04.050 --> 16:09.020
<i>However, with Will Serfort and 
Lady Elfaria as good as family,</i>

16:09.020 --> 16:12.180
<i>it's certain that anything she does 
would be seen as favoritism.</i>

16:14.320 --> 16:16.980
<i>Before Lady Elfaria explodes,</i>

16:16.980 --> 16:20.480
<i>is there any way to make an ally 
of another Magia Vander?</i>

16:22.580 --> 16:24.510
Talking is pointless.

16:27.470 --> 16:31.840
If we want to see the truth of this guy, 
there's a simple way to do it, right?

16:35.770 --> 16:37.020
Zeo?

16:37.460 --> 16:40.270
Hey, you rotten brat. One hit.

16:41.640 --> 16:43.880
Show me you can take one hit.

16:43.880 --> 16:47.290
If you can make it through this, 
I'll serve as your proof.

16:47.950 --> 16:50.490
Roar, Lightning Crash.

16:50.490 --> 16:52.420
<i>A super abbreviated chant?</i>

16:52.420 --> 16:54.240
<i>A low-level lightning spell?</i>

16:54.240 --> 16:55.990
Run, Will!

16:56.260 --> 16:58.280
Zalgia Saga.

17:02.500 --> 17:05.550
<i>There's no blocking that. No evading it.</i>

17:05.550 --> 17:07.530
<i>Which means I'll be obliterated.</i>

17:07.530 --> 17:09.090
<i>In order to survive...</i>

17:12.400 --> 17:16.510
Will!

17:25.020 --> 17:27.560
Fully charged...

17:29.830 --> 17:31.850
Zalgia Wis!

17:32.280 --> 17:34.550
A-A lightning mageblade?

17:34.550 --> 17:37.290
What's going on? What did he do?

17:37.630 --> 17:39.450
He ate the magic!

17:39.860 --> 17:44.220
The moment it struck, he charged 
his sword with it to halve the impact.

17:45.030 --> 17:47.550
Of course, he couldn't absorb all of it,

17:47.550 --> 17:51.360
so some of Zeo's colossal lightning
 scorched Will's insides,

17:51.360 --> 17:54.970
but he's shown he can withstand a kill shot
he could neither block nor evade.

18:01.660 --> 18:03.480
You went and survived, you rotten brat!

18:04.260 --> 18:05.980
You survived a hit from <i>me!</i>

18:06.380 --> 18:08.230
You all saw that, didn't you?!

18:08.230 --> 18:11.730
He took a shot from a Magia Vander 
and he's still standing!

18:12.240 --> 18:14.290
There's no better proof than that!

18:14.740 --> 18:16.850
I acknowledge you.

18:16.850 --> 18:19.240
You do not belong at the bottom.

18:19.710 --> 18:22.250
Make your way to the top, Will Serfort!

18:22.780 --> 18:25.260
Please wait, Lord Zeo!

18:25.260 --> 18:27.690
The Bloom is a solemn event 
where factions are decided.

18:27.690 --> 18:30.260
To advance via a method like this—

18:31.940 --> 18:34.510
Then you can take a shot
 from me too, right?

18:36.210 --> 18:39.760
There's no way he can do it 
and you can't, is there?

18:40.210 --> 18:42.180
If you don't survive this,

18:42.180 --> 18:45.520
there goes all your "proven worth,"
you glasses-wearing turd.

18:48.960 --> 18:53.650
I-I acknowledge 
Will Serfort's right to be here.

18:58.320 --> 19:00.160
Th-Then that means...

19:00.880 --> 19:02.160
Will Serfort!

19:02.870 --> 19:05.530
You are officially eligible to
be recruited into a faction!

19:12.540 --> 19:13.840
Lady Elfaria?!

19:19.030 --> 19:20.850
E-Elfie?!

19:20.850 --> 19:25.100
I'm so glad... I'm so glad!

19:31.740 --> 19:34.110
I'm sorry I couldn't do anything.

19:34.870 --> 19:36.970
Please don't apologize, Elfie.

19:37.510 --> 19:38.870
Smile instead.

19:42.080 --> 19:42.970
I'm here.

19:43.420 --> 19:45.800
I'm here where you've 
waited for me all this time.

19:56.940 --> 20:00.850
Elfie! I promise I'll make it 
to the tower, too!

20:00.850 --> 20:03.500
Let's go see the sunset together!

20:03.930 --> 20:05.080
I'll be waiting!

20:05.520 --> 20:08.230
As long as it takes!

20:10.850 --> 20:15.120
I've been waiting for you for so, so long.

21:41.610 --> 21:42.990
<b>Wistoria: Wand and Sword</b>

21:45.740 --> 21:51.250
There's really no need to ask, but what 
faction will you join, Will Serfort?

21:52.190 --> 21:53.420
I'll go to Elfie's—

21:53.420 --> 21:54.130
No.

21:56.110 --> 21:57.890
I'm taking this guy.

22:00.910 --> 22:04.900
What are you saying? Can't you read 
the room? Are you a fool? Are you stupid?

22:04.900 --> 22:08.770
Are you a thief? Are you a paramour? 
Are you a heretic? Are you a criminal?

22:08.130 --> 22:10.150
Elfie, calm down!

22:08.770 --> 22:11.030
Do you want to be frozen and destroyed?

22:11.100 --> 22:12.600
E-Elfie's faction—

22:13.600 --> 22:15.100
F-Faction...

22:17.650 --> 22:18.480
Will!

22:20.110 --> 22:21.820
Is that right?

22:21.820 --> 22:24.120
You want to join my faction?

22:24.120 --> 22:25.950
Then it's decided!

22:25.950 --> 22:27.700
You can't be serious!

22:28.030 --> 22:29.830
Release Will!

22:30.210 --> 22:33.040
Wh-What does this mean? What's going on?

22:33.040 --> 22:36.210
I guess it's a headhunting thing.

22:36.980 --> 22:39.340
Rose, i-if that's true...

22:39.700 --> 22:41.920
shouldn't the earth faction 
get in on this, too?!

22:41.920 --> 22:43.510
Will is really, really amazing!

22:43.510 --> 22:46.310
It's totally not because I want to be
 with him in the tower, too!

22:46.310 --> 22:47.920
Calm down, calm down.

22:48.650 --> 22:50.860
Just what are you trying to do, Zeo?

22:50.860 --> 22:54.270
You were never one 
to try to scout him, were you?

22:54.270 --> 22:56.410
I decided I want him.

22:56.410 --> 22:58.770
That's all. Isn't it obvious?

23:00.920 --> 23:04.980
You cannot shackle desire.
That's my personal code.

23:04.980 --> 23:08.960
Whether it's riches, alcohol, women, 
or guys... If I want 'em, I take 'em.

23:08.960 --> 23:11.740
If I don't, then I'm not being me.

23:11.740 --> 23:13.110
<i>Barbarian.</i>

23:13.500 --> 23:17.250
Oh, what beautiful, logical thinking!

23:18.520 --> 23:20.000
What a coincidence.

23:21.940 --> 23:25.880
Will is the one thing I don't 
intend to cede to anyone.

23:26.800 --> 23:30.250
And if anyone gets in my way,
 I'll pulverize them!

23:36.850 --> 23:39.650
Next time on <i>Wistoria: Wand and Sword</i>,

23:39.650 --> 23:42.810
episode 23, "A Roar of Ice and Lightning."

23:40.480 --> 23:45.990
Episode 23
 A Roar of Ice and Lightning
